"/metric-admission/"><span>19</span>Source metrics</a><a href="/subdivision/"><span>20</span>Subdivision</a><a href="/metric-selection/"><span>21</span>Metric selection</a><a href="/refinement-tower/"><span>22</span>Refinement tower</a><a href="/history-comparison/"><span>23</span>History comparison</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>Independent human review<br>pending</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Primary reading</div><h1>Four papers. Explicit claim boundaries.</h1><p class="lede">Current review editions from the living portal, preserved with their versions. Publication distributes a result; it does not complete independent review.</p></div><article class="paper-row"><div class="paper-number">I</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Paper I · 1.1.1</span><h2>Finite carriers and support flow</h2><p>Finite Tetrahedral Complexes, Skew Support Flow and Contact Readiness</p><p class="muted">Finite carriers, skew flow, unique-simplex gluing, spectra, ambient jumps and supplied readiness.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=PI">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md" download>Markdown ↓</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row"><div class="paper-number">II</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Paper II · 1.1.1</span><h2>Projective reconstruction</h2><p>Projective Reconstruction, Complex Phase Receipts and Frozen-Tree Validation</p><p class="muted">Real and complex phase receipts, parity ambiguities, frozen-tree validation and covariance.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_II_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=PII">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_II_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md" download>Markdown ↓</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row"><div class="paper-number">III</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Paper III · 1.1.1</span><h2>Symmetry, shells and collective mechanisms</h2><p>Tetrahedral Symmetry, Radial Spectra and Finite Collective Mechanisms</p><p class="muted">Signed symmetry, radial shells, prepared shapes, burden, retention and collective mechanisms.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_III_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=PIII">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_III_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md" download>Markdown ↓</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row"><div class="paper-number">IV</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Paper IV · 0.1</span><h2>Prepared controllers and renewal</h2><p>Finite Prepared Quantum Controllers, Capture Windows and Correlation-Preserving Renewal</p><p class="muted">Finite apparatus, history clocks, capture windows, joint errors and correlation-preserving renewal.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_IV_REVIEW_DRAFT_v0.1.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=PIV">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_IV_REVIEW_DRAFT_v0.1.md" download>Markdown ↓</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="curved-ground-v01"><div class="paper-number">G6</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>A stable nonzero curved matter orbit</h2><p>The unchanged action admits a stable scalar background with negative diamond holonomy.</p><p class="muted">Links U=-ib and positive lowest-mode matter give an exactly neutral relative equilibrium. At scalar rank, a constrained energy proof establishes nonlinear orbital stability for an explicit positive stiffness interval. A separate finite-rank theorem guarantees a stable minimizing set and forces nonflat minima at sufficiently small κ/(rN). Individual-orbit stability at higher rank remains open. 40 exact checks and two numerical campaigns; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/curved-ground-v0.1/UD_CURVED_GROUND_STABILITY_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/curved-ground-v0.1/UD_CURVED_GROUND_STABILITY_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=CGS01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="resonance-closure-v01"><div class="paper-number">G5</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>All six resonant cases closed</h2><p>Exact symmetry sectors complete the nonlinear instability theorem.</p><p class="muted">An S3 vertex-stabilizer sector and a C4 cyclic sector provide exactly Gauss-admissible, fixed-norm nonlinear departure witnesses at the six formerly excluded values. Together with the preceding proof, the specified nonzero neutral flat family is unstable for every a&gt;0 and κ≥0 at finite rank. 104 exact constructor checks and six numerical campaigns; independent review pending; unchanged candidate action; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/resonance-closure-v0.1/UD_RESONANCE_CLOSURE_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/resonance-closure-v0.1/UD_RESONANCE_CLOSURE_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=RSC01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="nonlinear-orbital-v01"><div class="paper-number">G4</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Nonlinear orbital instability</h2><p>Finite matter departure from arbitrarily small admissible perturbations.</p><p class="muted">An additional conserved Gram matrix and a force-canceling sector enable a controlled averaging proof. The nonzero neutral flat family is nonlinearly orbitally unstable within the unchanged candidate action except at six positive parameter values left open. The zero-matter vacuum stability theorem is preserved. 42 exact constructor checks; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/nonlinear-orbital-v0.1/UD_NONLINEAR_ORBITAL_INSTABILITY_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/nonlinear-orbital-v0.1/UD_NONLINEAR_ORBITAL_INSTABILITY_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=NOI01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="gauge-reduced-modes-v01"><div class="paper-number">G3</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Gauge-reduced modes and stability</h2><p>Exact mode frequencies, persistent Jordan chains, and a stable vacuum gauge orbit.</p><p class="muted">The nonzero neutral flat family has 86 real reduced dimensions in the Abelian branch. Its imaginary spectrum retains nongauge secular growth for every positive diamond stiffness. A separate conserved-functional proof establishes nonlinear vacuum stability. Higher-rank slice modes retain their residual stabilizer constraint. Candidate action; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/gauge-reduced-modes-v0.1/UD_GAUGE_REDUCED_MODES_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/gauge-reduced-modes-v0.1/UD_GAUGE_REDUCED_MODES_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=GRM01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="joint-hamiltonian-v01"><div class="paper-number">G2</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Gauss closure and reciprocal dynamics</h2><p>A constrained joint link–matter Hamiltonian with an exact neutral curvature seed.</p><p class="muted">A declared classical U(r) action preserves matrix Gauss law, total energy and both matter norms, with global temporal-gauge flow. A dynamical opposite-charge partner admits nonzero neutral initial states. Their backreaction can leave the flat-link sector. Action and species selection, physical group and correspondence remain open. Physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/joint-hamiltonian-v0.1/UD_JOINT_HAMILTONIAN_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/joint-hamiltonian-v0.1/UD_JOINT_HAMILTONIAN_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=GHT01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="gauge-transport-v01"><div class="paper-number">G1</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Gauge-covariant incidence transport</h2><p>A flatness theorem and an exact phase-controlled spectrum.</p><p class="muted">Unitary transport on the 28 Hasse links preserves support and gauge covariance. Retaining the transport chain identity forces flatness on the filled tetrahedron. A one-link phase gives a conditional spectral splitting. Source-selected group, gauge-field action, continuum and physical correspondence remain open.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/gauge-transport-v0.1/UD_GAUGE_TRANSPORT_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/gauge-transport-v0.1/UD_GAUGE_TRANSPORT_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=GBT01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="narrative-v015"><div class="paper-number">N</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Additional workstream · review candidate 0.15</span><h2>Distinction, interaction and persistence</h2><p>A separate 56-page theoretical synthesis by Benjamin Walker Mayes, dated 15 October 2026 UTC.</p><p class="muted">Ingested source: gluing and dynamic memory, noisy access, finite records, sampled events and receipt-error limits. Its claims retain their stated assumptions; companion replay packages were not supplied for this intake. Independent review remains pending. Physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/narrative-v0.15/UD_Theory_Narrative_Manuscript_v0.15.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=N015">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/narrative-v0.15/INTAKE_v0.1.md">Intake receipt ↓</a></div></div></article><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">05</div><div><h2>Reproduction and review.</h2><p>Every imported source retains its own constructor-check record. The new atlas additionally verifies three core incidence constructions with exact arithmetic; that check is limited to boundary identities, skew symmetry, spectra and simplex counts.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/sources/UD_ATLAS_CORE_VERIFICATION_v0.1.json">Atlas check receipt ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/verify_core.py" download>Exact checker ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_Exact_Reproduction_v1.0_2026-09-16.zip" download>Earlier exact reproduction package ↓</a></div><p class="muted">The earlier v1.0 package is retained as an earlier replay object, not relabeled as a full verifier for the later papers.</p></div></section></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public reading edition 0.14</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribution</a><a href="https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/">Living research portal ↗</a></div><p class="footer-rule">Proof, simulation and physical correspondence retain distinct evidence status. Physical promotion: 0.</p></footer></div></body></html>
