+# Result
+
+The curved scalar branch is nonlinearly orbitally stable exactly for 0<=kappa<=4N*w0/Lambda_plus and unstable for larger kappa, conditional on the unchanged action, fixed N_psi=N_chi=N>0 and a>0. Here w0=rho*(10-sqrt(10))/480, rho=sqrt(8+2sqrt(10)), Lambda_plus=(28+17sqrt(10)+sqrt(866-128sqrt(10)))/18; kappa_star/N is approximately 0.03760248457.
+
+The fixed-norm gauge/phase reduction has 84 real dimensions. Fourteen neutral matter frequencies are rho±sqrt(8-2sqrt(10)) once each, 2rho once, rho±2 three times each, and rho five times. Twenty-eight charged link-charge pairs are specified by exact small-block determinant pencils. Every squared charged frequency is real because the mass matrix is positive.
+
+The first crossing is threefold standard-representation softening. At equality there are three zero Jordan chains, yet the orbit is nonlinearly stable: a matter-relaxed quartic is positive, certified by exact outward-rounded integer intervals. Above equality a real growing mode produces constrained nonlinear orbital departure.
+
+47 exact constructor checks, four numerical linear benchmarks and three nonlinear campaigns passed. Independent review and additional color modes remain open. No action change or experimental data; physical promotion 0.
